  "paper_limitation": "The chance-level stiffness/contact curves in outputs/metrics.json are not evidence of representation failure: they use n_val=12 (3-way probe, binomial SE\u22480.14). On the 2000-episode MLS-MPM dump (n_val=200, balanced 67/67/66), contact-quadrant linear probes reliably beat chance (~0.57 vs 0.25). Stiffness class and continuous Young's-modulus regression stay at chance (acc\u22480.34 vs 0.33; R\u00b2\u22480), including an oracle probe on z_target, and train accuracy is also near chance (~0.35). z_target occupies a near-constant shell (||z|| std\u22481e-4; all 128 dims have std\u226a\u03b3=1, so the VICReg variance hinge is binding). We report stiffness non-decodability as a limitation of the current encoder rather than suppressing it. Caveat: the physics VICReg checkpoint is from early workshop training, not the finished 200-epoch run; contact-above-chance already shows the scaled probe is powered. A workshop MSE checkpoint was not yet available."
